From c465ddd148dd8788c82514aad537c9b732f39011 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vasiliy Kovalev <kovalev@altlinux.org>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 14:31:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] xt_DELUDE: force a real dst reference before cloning
 input route

delude_send_reset() runs from the LOCAL_IN hook (target .hooks includes
NF_INET_LOCAL_IN) and does skb_dst_set(nskb, dst_clone(skb_dst(oldskb))). On the
input path skb_dst(oldskb) can be a no-ref dst (SKB_DST_NOREF, refcount 0), so
dst_hold() inside dst_clone() warns (include/net/dst.h) and, with panic_on_warn,
panics. Force the input skb's dst to hold a real reference with skb_dst_force()
before cloning it, mirroring nf_reject_ipv4's handling; drop the reply if no dst
is available.

Signed-off-by: Vasiliy Kovalev <kovalev@altlinux.org>
---
 extensions/xt_DELUDE.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/extensions/xt_DELUDE.c b/extensions/xt_DELUDE.c
index ba913cf..327acc5 100644
--- a/extensions/xt_DELUDE.c
+++ b/extensions/xt_DELUDE.c
@@ -122,7 +122,13 @@ static void delude_send_reset(struct sk_buff *oldskb,
 #endif
 		addr_type = RTN_LOCAL;
 
-	/* ip_route_me_harder expects skb->dst to be set */
+	/*
+	 * ip_route_me_harder() expects skb->dst to be set. On the LOCAL_IN hook
+	 * the input dst may be reference-free (SKB_DST_NOREF, refcount 0), and
+	 * dst_clone()/dst_hold() on it warns. Force a real reference first.
+	 */
+	if (skb_dst(oldskb) == NULL || !skb_dst_force(oldskb))
+		goto free_nskb;
 	skb_dst_set(nskb, dst_clone(skb_dst(oldskb)));
 	if (ip_route_me_harder(par_net(par), par->state->sk, nskb, addr_type))
 		goto free_nskb;
